Render external-tool artifacts. Without --input-dir or --output-dir, print this help. Context-free rendering requires both paths and conflicts with --context and --sensitive. Context-backed rendering requires --output-dir and --sensitive. This command is recognized but not implemented.

Usage:
  bootwright render [flags]
  bootwright render [command]

Available Commands:
  effective   Show normalized effective desired state
  installer   Render container-cluster installer artifacts (unavailable)
  storage     Render storage artifacts (unavailable)

Flags:
      --clusters string     Select comma-separated cluster names (default: all)
      --input-dir string    Read a context-free input file or directory
      --output string       Select output mode (values: text, json) (default "text")
      --output-dir string   Write artifacts to the selected directory
      --sensitive           Authorize sensitive artifact materialization

Global Flags:
      --context string             Select a context (default: current context)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines

Use "bootwright render [command] --help" for more information about a command.
